    {
      "entryId": "ramcharitmanas-bala-kanda-0111",
      "sequence": 123,
      "meaning": "Pārvatī further asks for the truth in which wise sages become immersed in realization, and for devotion, knowledge, realization and detachment explained with all their divisions. She requests every other secret of Rāma with utterly pure discernment and asks the compassionate Lord not to hide even what she failed to ask. The Vedas call him teacher of the three worlds; what could another lowly creature know? Śiva delights in Umā’s naturally lovely, guileless questions. All Rāma’s deeds arise in Hara’s heart; love thrills his body and fills his eyes with tears. Raghunātha’s form appears within, bringing immeasurable supreme bliss. Absorbed in meditation’s nectar for two watches, Maheśa brings his mind outward and joyfully begins Raghupati’s story.",
